0: megatron:    ' in the library."\n\n  "I should like to see her father," said Glynn, as she returned to the door. "He is so good and kind, and so very inquisitive."\n\n  "I shall know if he is ever to see you again," said Elsie, as she walked slowly up the broad staircase.\n\n  "Ah, I shall see you again, my dear, when I have not seen you for a long time," said Glynn, as she was off again, with her head in the air, and a new light in her eyes.\n\n  "Ah, dear, you are not going to be happy, are you?" said Lambert, as he seated himself on the bench outside.\n\n  " I am going to see my father, if you please, and see if I can\'t see him to-night," returned Elsie.\n\n  "I am not going to see him now," replied Glynn, "if he is coming to see me."\n\n  "Ah, dear, I am not going to see him. I have a father, you know."\n\n  "I am not going to see him, if you please, Elsie."\n\n  "I am not going to see him, I am going to see my father," said the girl, with a little sigh, and a look of kindly contentment.\n\n  "Oh, my fat
